{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Resolution discovered during plan review\n\nNo production change is warranted. A4-1 already solved the operational defect at the correct boundary and deliberately preserved the raw differ contract.\n\nThe raw `compute_mutations(local_state, jira_state)` API must treat its first argument as real local state. For `local_state = {\"RB-8\": {}}` and `jira_state = {\"RB-8\": {\"summary\": \"remote\"}}`, it emits a `field_drift` update. That behavior is a load-bearing positive control for callers that honor the API contract.\n\nThe sole production snapshot caller does not honor that contract: it passes `prev_snapshot` and `curr_snapshot`, both remote Jira state. A4-1, merged as Gerrit 1256 / `6cdd4b00d9ee` with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, filters differ-owned `field_drift` and `unbound_local` emissions immediately at that call site. The source and tests explicitly require the filter to remain there so a future migration to real local state can remove it without weakening the pure differ.\n\nChanging `_compute_mutations_emit_both` as originally proposed would contradict that decision and break the raw-differ positive control. This ticket therefore verifies the already-landed behavior and records the no-change decision.\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- Run `test_key_set_prev_field_drift_never_survives_the_production_filter`; it proves the raw positive control emits and the production call-site result contains zero outbound updates.\n- Run `test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create` and `test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression`; they prove the filter does not swallow genuine work or invariant repairs.\n- Run the converged `reconcile_once` and real-repository idempotency tests; they prove persisted `mutation_count == 0`.\n- Execute an in-session counting probe around the real production path with a key-set previous snapshot. Prove the counter observes a representative `git rev-parse` call in its positive control, then assert zero per-mutation calls after the A4-1 filter.\n- Record exact commands and outcomes on this ticket and the epic session log. No source, test, or documentation file is changed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The raw differ emits its documented field-drift positive control while the production snapshot call-site result contains zero outbound updates for the same key-set entry.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Genuine inbound-create and invariant-seed mutations survive the call-site filter.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A converged pass records `mutation_count == 0`.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An instrumented production-path probe records exactly zero per-mutation `git rev-parse` calls and its positive control proves the counter is live.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The no-change decision, A4-1 Gerrit evidence, commands, and results are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## File impact\n\nNone. A4-1 already contains the production filter and load-bearing characterization tests.","title":"A4-3 verification: accept A4-1 call-site suppression and make no differ change"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785774664392827001,"uuid":"b49d50da-b8d7-49f7-bcc7-bf1400fa998c"}